# CVE suppressions for casky-runner
#
# Policy: suppress only when (a) no fixed version exists in the npm registry yet,
# and (b) the vulnerable code path is unreachable in this container at runtime.
# Re-evaluate monthly or when Trivy reports a published fixed version.

# minimatch: ReDoS via crafted glob patterns
# CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904 — fixed in 10.2.3 (not yet published to npm)
# minimatch is used internally by @anthropic-ai/claude-code and @google/gemini-cli
# for file-system pattern matching. The runner accepts no untrusted glob input.
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# picomatch: ReDoS via crafted extglob patterns
# CVE-2026-33671 — fixed in 4.0.4 (not yet published to npm)
# Same usage context as minimatch above.
CVE-2026-33671

# tar: path traversal via drive-relative linkpath / symlink traversal
# CVE-2026-29786, CVE-2026-31802 — fixed in 7.5.10/7.5.11 (not yet published to npm)
# tar is used by npm to extract packages at image build time only.
# The runner does not extract untrusted archives at runtime.
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
